# herdr, forked because an agent behind a pty proxy is invisible to the agents panel.
#
# herdr names the agent in a pane by listing one process group, the foreground group of the
# pane's own terminal. A pty proxy holds that terminal and runs the shell on a second one in a
# session of its own, so the agent is a descendant of the pane process and can never be in the
# group herdr lists. The shell autocomplete here is exactly that shape, so every session behind
# it was missing from the panel.
#
# Upstream does not take outside pull requests. The walk was offered by another user and closed
# by a bot in nine seconds without being read, and the issue behind it was closed as needing
# design rather than a fix. decisions/herdr-agent-detection.md carries the whole record, the
# links are under watch below, and forks/CLAUDE.md carries the rule for when this fork goes.
name      | herdr
upstream  | https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr.git
fork      | https://github.com/milosdjakovic/herdr.git
base      | v0.9.0
pin       | 4ef0ba8bce0995ad2028f560b422d9ccd24ed136
dest      | .local/bin/herdr
decisions | decisions/herdr-agent-detection.md

# One branch, two commits. The first is the other user's, cherry picked with their authorship
# intact, since it is their work under Apache 2.0. The second is the test it lacked, because
# the only wrapper test upstream had spawns its agent as a background job of the same shell,
# which never leaves the pane's process group and so was already passing before the walk.
patch | feat/detect-agents-in-descendant-process-groups | a descendant walk, so an agent in a child process group is identified when the pane's own foreground group holds none | https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr/pull/3176

